 redirect to a different origin (host). This allows sensitive authentication
 credentials to be inadvertently exposed to third-party hosts during HTTP
 redirects. The fix adds a check to ensure that Authorization credentials
 are only sent when the redirect target host matches the original request host.
Origin: vendor, SUSE wget-do-not-propagate-credentials.patch
Author: Security Team
Bug: https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?56909
Last-Update: 2025-12-23

